{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>They shall be ashamed</b> — When they see my life restored, they themselves shall be dismayed; therefore <i>they shall be terrified</i> corresponds to <i>I am terrified</i>, and my soul is greatly terrified." "<b>They shall turn back</b> — They shall be comforted, or they shall seek my wellbeing."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "Resolved the root בהל consistently as 'terrified' to preserve the wordplay between נבהלו and נבהל, though Ibn Ezra may intend a nuance of 'dismayed' in the first instance and 'terrified' in the second."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:27.132506771Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}